2.  I am solving the problem by first determining the number of files that were not deleted, which can be found by subtracting the number of deleted files from the total number of files. 3.  This result is then divided by the number of files in each folder to find the number of folders.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The number of files Nancy deleted is 31.
    \item The number of files remaining is $80 - 31 = 49$.
    \item The number of folders is $49 \div 7 = 7$.
\end{enumerate}
Therefore, Nancy ended up with 7 folders.

\boxed{7}

