A florist had 50 roses. If she sold 15 of them and then later picked 21 more, how many roses would she have?
The florist started with 50 roses.
She sold 15 roses, so the number of roses left is 50 - 15 = 35 roses.
She picked 21 more roses, so the number of roses she has is 35 + 21 = 56 roses.

So, the final answer is 56.

